{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The fixed shape of CLAUDE.md. Enforced by scripts/check_claude_md_size.py.",
    "",
    "Each section carries a `target` and a `budget`, and they mean different things:",
    "  target -- the size this section was trimmed TO. Targets sum to <= HARD_TOTAL_BUDGET.",
    "  budget -- what CI enforces: target + ~5% working room, so a one-word fix to a row is not",
    "            a build failure. Budgets sum to well under the harness cap.",
    "",
    "It is a ratchet, the same shape .ruff-baseline uses: a budget may only ever move DOWN, and",
    "`budget >= target` always. The two ceilings that make the ratchet meaningful --",
    "HARD_TOTAL_BUDGET and MAX_SECTION_BUDGET -- are CONSTANTS IN THE LINTER, not fields here, so",
    "relaxing the guard means editing code and its unit test in the same PR rather than nudging a",
    "number in a data file.",
    "",
    "The working room is for FIXING a row, not for growing the file. Growth is supposed to go into",
    "the docs/*.md a row points at; max_rows and row_max are what enforce that."
  ],
  "root": "CLAUDE.md",
  "doc_index": "docs/README.md",
  "nested_cap": 12000,
  "extra_caps": {
    ".github/copilot-instructions.md": 9000
  },
  "default_row_max": 320,
  "reference_row_max": 140,
  "cm019_level": "error",
  "preamble": {
    "budget": 70,
    "target": 60
  },
